  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown below, the key is pressed at time t = 0. Which of the following statement(s) is(are) true?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_13.jpg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "q2ObU",
      "text": "The voltmeter displays -5V as soon as the key is pressed, and displays +5V after a long time",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "n0Lcg",
      "text": "The voltmeter will display 0 V at time t = ln 2 seconds",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rqgiJ",
      "text": "The current in the ammeter becomes 1/e of the initial value after 1 second",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25Z22",
      "text": "The current in the ammeter becomes zero after a long time",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i) At t = 0, capacitor acts as short - circuit<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_13_Ans_a_.jpg\"/></p><p>The the reading of voltmeter will be -5 V<br >At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math> capacitor acts as open circuit and no current flows through voltmeter.<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_13_Ans_b_.jpg\"/><br/>If it is ideal voltmeter then its resistance is infinite & therefore it will read +5V<br >(ii)<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_13_Ans_c_.jpg\"/></p><p>The Charge on the capacitor is given by<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>RC</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math><br/>as q<sub>0</sub> = RC is the max charge stored</p><p>For C<span style=\"font-size: 10.8333px;\">1</span>=2C=40 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi></math>F, R<span style=\"font-size: 10.8333px;\">1</span>=R=25 k<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>CV</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>CR</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>  </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math></p><p>The current through resistance of R=25 k is </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>CR</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>For C<sub>2</sub>=C=20 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi></math>F, R<sub>2</sub>=2R=50 k<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>CV</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>CR</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math></p><p>The current through resistance of 2R=50k is </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>CR</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>Reading of voltmeter (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo></math>V) = Voltage across 2C - Voltage across 2R</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>CR</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><br/>(iii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>RC</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>sec</mi></math><br/>Now Current is given by<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>at t= 1 sec, Current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><br/>(iv) After long time no current flows since capacitor act as a open circuit and voltmeter acts as an ideal it's resistance is infinite, therefore current does not allow.</p>",
